  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Indiana total $4.1B for FY2026 to date. The federal government issued 19,933 awards, with an average award size of $205K. Obligations are down 41.8% year over year. Historical context shows FY21 obligations at $6.3B, FY22 obligations at $8.2B, FY23 obligations at $6B, FY24 obligations at $5.3B, and FY25 obligations at $7B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in the state, obligating $2.8B so far in FY2026. Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $894M. Top vendors include ROLLS-ROYCE CORPORATION with $975M and WELLPOINT FEDERAL SOLUTIONS, INC. with $270M. The FY2026 to date totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove FY2026 federal obligations in Indiana?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $2.8B and is the primary driver of FY2026 obligations. Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing recorded $894M in obligations, reflecting concentrated industry spending. The state recorded 19,933 awards with an average award size of $205K, which together shape the overall obligations total of $4.1B. Obligations are down 41.8% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2026 spending in Indiana?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads agency buying with $2.8B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $356M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $301M. ROLLS-ROYCE CORPORATION is the largest vendor with $975M, followed by WELLPOINT FEDERAL SOLUTIONS, INC. with $270M and LMI CONSULTING, LLC with $252M. Several industries concentrate spending, including Engineering Services at $364M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $316M."
      }
    ]
  },
