      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Indiana?",
      "a": "The state received $4.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The total reflects 19,933 awards and an average award size of $205K. Obligations are down 41.8% year over year. FY21 obligations were $6.3B, FY22 obligations were $8.2B, FY23 obligations were $6B, FY24 obligations were $5.3B, and FY25 obligations were $7B."
